Z||000022||fogglethorpe||11-07-2001||05:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tigger:<BR><B>When will new bands start writing [b]new</B> songs?  Recording re-makes seems to be the latest fad.<P>It's crazy when the only song from an album worth playing on the air is the re-make of an old one.  To me, it shows the band is weak - a one hit (re-make) wonder.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>I agree for the most part, but there are a few exceptions...notably, Tori Amos' "Strange Little Girls", which is all remakes. But, she reworked them in such a way as to render them unrecognizable from the originals. The songs become almost hers.<P>There is an outrageous version of Neil Young's "Heart of Gold" that's quite cool.<P>||||reg||1
